@@ -11,6 +11,12 @@ editable copy of the project or conversation: the native `AgentHost` is
 authoritative, and every reload re-runs the handshake and reconstructs the
 page from the host's `state` message.

+The page, not the web view, decides when the handshake ends. A navigation the
+web view starts may fail and leave the page in place, or come back to it from
+the back-forward cache without loading it again. So the page sends
+`page_hidden` when its document goes, and sends `hello` again when the cache
+restores it.
+
 ## Building

 CMake builds this page whenever an input changes (`npm ci` from the lockfile, then `npm run build`). The output is `resources/jusprin/agent/index.html`; it is generated, not committed. Node/npm is required unless you configure with `-DJUSPRIN_BUILD_WEB=OFF` and supply that file yourself.
